## What is established (do not re-derive; the previous job's Core-bug conclusion was WRONG)
- Read `doc/plan/c016-worklog/bucketB-dotnet-stale-summary.md` for the traces, but its classification
  "Core defect" is overruled by the spec text below. Core behaves per spec.
- `core/doc/spec/core/socket/README.ko.md` §4 "rid 중복 정책" (HANDOVER): when opposite-direction pipes
  of the same peer RID conflict, both peers compare RIDs and pick ONE direction; a request already
  admitted on the losing direction is not carried over — "그 request의 reply는 submit 시점에 사용한
  바로 그 transport pair로만 전달되도록 제한되어 있어 request를 완료하지 못하고, request는 자기
  timeout으로 정확히 한 번 종결된다. **Caller는 handover 뒤 다시 보낸다.**"
- `framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/02-channel-transport/01-channel-topology.ko.md` "Peer 연결":
  automatic RouteMesh — only the smaller-RID node connects; "Manual 양방향 connect와 automatic의 연결
  경합·오래된 후보는 같은 handshake와 duplicate-pipe admission을 거쳐 **ready 연결 하나만** 남긴다."
- Core impl (`core/src/runtime/sockets/router/router_admission.cpp` identify_peer, `reciprocal_duplicate`):
  the losing pipe stays alive as an anonymous standby RID (`_standby_pipes`); only the winner carries the
  logical RID. ROUTER-ROUTER = one lane set (Application + Completion lane).
- The three failing tests (`StatefulServiceRuntimeTests.RemoteActorStaleAuthority*`) register both
  peers, start caller then owner, both `ConnectPeer` each other (manual bilateral), wait for
  `AdmittedPeerCount == 1` on both, then `RequestToActor(..., 3 s)`. Trace: owner replies OK on the
  winner's Completion lane; caller's pending request is pinned to the loser pair → discarded per spec →
  `ExpireOperationAsync` TimedOut(101). The framework's own duplicate handling logged
  `mesh_peer_duplicate_retire` + `mesh_peer_duplicate_retire_skip_transport` (keeps the loser transport as
  standby, `SharesNativeHandoverRoute`).
- So the defect is one of: (a) the framework declares the peer Admitted/ready and submits application
  requests **before Core's handover has settled** (framework spec: "ready 연결 하나만 남긴다"), and/or
  (b) the framework does not **resend after handover** as the Core spec requires of the caller. The node
  framework's terminal-replay loop and the cpp framework's bilateral survivor handling
  (`test_cpp_framework_m6a_runtime.cpp` `verify_duplicate_connection_survivor_is_symmetric`,
  `verify_bilateral_raw_connection_without_public_pipe_id_keeps_survivor`) are the parity references.
- Also note: Core main now includes D-B85 (`7d8205a028`): DONTWAIT REQUEST can return BACKPRESSURED +
  wait token; the .NET binding's REQUEST port for that is NOT done yet (B's job). Do not build on it;
  if you observe BACKPRESSURED on request submit, report it and keep to the handover cause.
- Env: `core/build-dev` and `.artifacts/wsl` are being rebuilt for the new Core right now; wait until
  `/home/hep7/project/zlink/zlink-work/c016/logs/rebuild-newcore.done` exists before running dotnet
  tests. dotnet test env block (never `--artifacts-path`, never `ulimit -v`):
  `export TMPDIR=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-dotnet ZLINK_LIBRARY_PATH=/home/hep7/project/zlink/core/build-dev/lib UseSharedCompilation=false MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE=1 DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1; pkg_hash=$(sha256sum .artifacts/wsl/nuget/Systems.Zlink.0.17.0.nupkg | awk '{print $1}'); export NUGET_PACKAGES=/dev/shm/zlink-tmp-dotnet/nuget-${pkg_hash:0:16}; cd framework/languages/dotnet; flock -w7200 /tmp/zlink-dotnet-gate.lock dotnet test tests/Zlink.Framework.UnitTests --filter '...'`.
